# Design System for Style

When writing or editing code that involves **style** (colors, typography, spacing, theming), follow this project's design system.

## Source of truth

- **Flutter (mobile)**: `mobile/lib/shared/theme/app_theme.dart`
  - `AppTheme.light` / `AppTheme.dark` define `ThemeData` with `ColorScheme`, `textTheme`, and theme extensions.
  - **Typography**: `textTheme` is built from `Typography.material2021(colorScheme)` (Material 2021 type scale). Light theme uses `.black`, dark uses `.white`; colors come from `colorScheme`. To add a brand font later, derive `textTheme` with `.apply(fontFamily: '...')` in `_textTheme`.

## Do

- **Colors**: Use `Theme.of(context).colorScheme` (e.g. `primary`, `onSurface`, `surfaceContainerHighest`, `onSurfaceVariant`, `outline`, `error`, `onError`). For accounting/chart/hero-card semantics, use the theme extensions:
  - `AccountingColors.of(context)` → `income`, `expense`, `transfer`, `borrow`, `repay`, `liability`, `neutral`
  - `ChartPalette.of(context)` → `palette` for charts
  - `HeroCardColors.of(context)` → `content`, `contentMuted`, `shadowSubtle`
- **Typography**: Use `Theme.of(context).textTheme` (e.g. `displayLarge`, `headlineMedium`, `titleMedium`, `bodyLarge`, `bodySmall`, `labelLarge`). Adjust only when needed via `copyWith(color: ...)` using theme colors.
- **Opacity**: Prefer `colorScheme.onSurfaceVariant.withValues(alpha: 0.5)` (or similar) over hardcoded transparent colors.
- **New tokens**: Add new colors or semantic tokens in `app_theme.dart` (and to the right extension or `ColorScheme`), then reference them via theme in UI code.

## Don't

- Don't hardcode `Color(0xFF...)` or `Colors.xxx` in UI widgets; use theme/context so light/dark and semantics stay consistent.
- Don't hardcode font family or ad-hoc `TextStyle(fontSize: ..., fontWeight: ...)` in UI; use `textTheme` and override only when needed (e.g. `copyWith(color: ...)`).
- Don't define parallel color or text-style constants in feature code; keep a single source in `app_theme.dart`.
